	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Burning Steppes are a country of ash. Between the {link:redridge-mountains}Redridge Mountains{/link} to the south and the smoking bulk of {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link} to the north-west, the land lies black and broken, veined with rivers of molten stone. Nothing green grows here for long. The air tastes of cinders, the sky glows red by night, and the ground itself is warm underfoot. Yet the Steppes are no empty waste. They are the only road on foot between the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link} and the dwarven lands of Khaz Modan beyond the mountain, and every power that covets that road has come to hold a piece of it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Steppes were not always a waste. The scholars of {link:morgan-s-vigil}Morgan's Vigil{/link} say that the land was once the northern end of the {link:redridge-mountains}Redridge{/link} range, with the same red ridges and cold streams that {link:lakeshire}Lakeshire{/link} still knows. It was the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} who ended that. Exiled from {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} after the war of the three dwarven clans, they built a city in these mountains and named it for their sorcerer-thane, {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link}. When the Bronzebeards and the Wildhammers marched against them, Thaurissan reached into the depths of the world for a weapon, and he called up {red:ragnaros}Ragnaros{/red} the Firelord instead. The coming of Ragnaros melted the mountains for leagues around. The Dark Iron city was ruined, a volcano rose where the land had split, and the country to its south burned. It has never stopped burning.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The Steppes belong to no crown. The orcs of the {link:blackrock-clan}Blackrock clan{/link} hold the heart of the land from their stronghold beneath the mountain, and their war bands go south through {link:blackrock-pass}Blackrock Pass{/link} to trouble {link:lakeshire}Lakeshire{/link}. Firegut ogres guard the mines of {link:dreadmaul-rock}Dreadmaul Rock{/link} for them. Black dragonkin nest along the eastern cliffs and in the scorched hills of the south-west. Dark Iron spies and firewalkers still haunt the ruins of their old city, and living fire and stone walk the plains.

Against all of this, {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Stormwind{/link} keeps a single outpost: {link:morgan-s-vigil}Morgan's Vigil{/link}, on a ridge in the south-east, where {link:marshal-maxwell}Marshal Maxwell{/link} holds out with a handful of soldiers and scholars and waits for a regent who does not send an army. The marshal who once commanded them, {red:reginald-windsor}Reginald Windsor{/red}, has been lost in the mountain with all his gathered knowledge of the enemy. Far to the north, beneath the ridge, a small camp at {link:flame-crest}Flame Crest{/link} shelters traders, seekers and outcasts of every people, and gives the {link:horde}Horde{/link} a foothold of its own.

What the watchers of the Vigil have begun to learn is that the orcs are not the true masters of the Steppes. Something older and far more cunning moves the {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link} from behind, and its claws may reach further than anyone in {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} wishes to believe.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:blackrock-clan}Blackrock orcs{/link}.{/b} The oldest of the war clans, still keeping the ways of the old {link:horde}Horde{/link}. Their soldiers, sorcerers and warlocks fill the central plains and the fortress beneath the mountain, and their worgs run with them.
• {b}The Firegut ogres.{/b} Allies of the {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link}, they hold {link:dreadmaul-rock}Dreadmaul Rock{/link} and keep its supply lines open.
• {b}The black dragonkin.{/b} Broodlings, dragonspawn, wyrmkin and drakes roam the eastern cliffs and {link:terror-wing-path}Terror Wing Path{/link}. Their flame-scaled kin hold {link:draco-dar}Draco'dar{/link} in the south-west.
• {b}The {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link}.{/b} Spies, agents and firewalkers of {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link} watch over the ruined city, and war reavers of their making stalk the ashes.
• {b}The children of fire.{/b} Obsidian and flame elementals wander the land, remnants of the fire that made it.
• {b}The people of {link:morgan-s-vigil}Morgan's Vigil{/link}.{/b} Soldiers of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}, a {link:night-elves}night elf{/link} scout, a {link:gnomes}gnome{/link} of the mages and an agent of the nobility, all holding one ridge.
• {b}The folk of {link:flame-crest}Flame Crest{/link}.{/b} Goblin traders, a gnome treasure seeker, an elven enchanter, a drunken {link:dwarves}dwarf{/link} and the orcs of the Horde, sheltering together beneath the northern ridge.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Green Country.{/b} Long ago the Steppes were part of the {link:redridge-mountains}Redridge{/link} range, and the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} raised their city among its peaks.
• {b}The Summoning.{/b} Sorcerer-Thane {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link} called up Ragnaros. The mountains melted, {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link} was born, and the land became the Burning Steppes.
• {b}The Wars of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.{/b} The orcs made the mountain their fortress. In the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} came north to besiege it, and at the foot of Blackrock Spire {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link} slew {link:anduin-lothar}Anduin Lothar{/link}. {link:turalyon}Turalyon{/link} took up Lothar's command and broke the Horde.
• {b}The Return of the Blackrock.{/b} The Blackrock who escaped the internment camps went back to the mountain that bears their name, and they have held the Steppes ever since.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} Marshal Windsor gathered proof of who truly commands the Blackrock, and he vanished before he could deliver it. {link:morgan-s-vigil}Morgan's Vigil{/link} keeps watch, and waits.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Steppes",
			text = [=[• The {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link} relics that litter the ruined city are said to hold memories of the summoning. Those who touch them carry away visions of the day the mountain was born.
• At {link:morgan-s-vigil}the Vigil{/link}, the soldiers speak of Ironfoe, the hammer that Marshal Windsor carried. They say it was forged by a Dark Iron master for an ancestor of his, and that it has a twin.
• The orcs of the Steppes breed and train their worgs within {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link} Spire. No matter how many are slain, the packs never seem to grow smaller.
• In the camp at {link:flame-crest}Flame Crest{/link}, a goblin and a {link:gnomes}gnome{/link} argue over dragon eggs, a goblin sells worg pups to the rich, and a sister hunts her own brother for the price on his head.]=],
		},
	},
})

